# Emergency Response App - Bolt.new Implementation Plan

## 🎯 Project Overview
Build a disaster-agnostic emergency response platform that handles multiple emergency types (earthquakes, wildfires, floods, medical crises, etc.) with real-time SOS submissions, volunteer coordination, and resource management.

---

## 📊 Database Schema & Tables

### 1. Emergency Types Table
```sql
Table: emergency_types
- id (Primary Key, Auto-increment)
- type_name (Text): "Earthquake", "Wildfire", "Flood", "Medical", "Industrial", etc.
- description (Long Text)
- icon_url (Text): URL to emergency type icon
- color_code (Text): Hex color for UI theming
- is_active (Boolean): Enable/disable emergency types
- created_at (DateTime)
```

### 2. Emergencies Table
```sql
Table: emergencies
- id (Primary Key, Auto-increment)
- emergency_type_id (Foreign Key → emergency_types.id)
- title (Text): Brief emergency description
- description (Long Text): Detailed emergency information
- severity_level (Number): 1-10 scale
- latitude (Number): GPS coordinates
- longitude (Number): GPS coordinates
- address (Text): Human-readable location
- status (Dropdown): "Active", "In Progress", "Resolved", "Closed"
- submitter_name (Text)
- submitter_phone (Text)
- submitter_email (Email)
- photo_urls (JSON Array): URLs to uploaded photos
- resources_needed (JSON Array): List of required resources
- volunteers_needed (Number): How many volunteers required
- priority_level (Dropdown): "Low", "Medium", "High", "Critical"
- estimated_affected_people (Number)
- created_at (DateTime)
- updated_at (DateTime)
- resolved_at (DateTime)
```

### 3. Volunteers Table
```sql
Table: volunteers
- id (Primary Key, Auto-increment)
- full_name (Text)
- email (Email, Unique)
- phone (Text)
- password_hash (Text): Encrypted password
- profile_photo_url (Text)
- skills (Multi-Select): "Medical", "Search & Rescue", "Fire Safety", "HAZMAT", "Heavy Machinery", "Logistics", "Translation", "Counseling", "IT Support", "Engineering"
- availability_status (Dropdown): "Available", "Busy", "Offline"
- current_latitude (Number): Real-time location
- current_longitude (Number): Real-time location
- max_travel_distance (Number): Kilometers willing to travel
- emergency_contacts (JSON): Emergency contact information
- certifications (JSON Array): Professional certifications
- languages_spoken (Multi-Select): Language capabilities
- rating (Number): 1-5 star rating from past responses
- total_responses (Number): Count of emergency responses
- is_verified (Boolean): Background check status
- created_at (DateTime)
- last_active (DateTime)
```

### 4. Emergency Assignments Table
```sql
Table: emergency_assignments
- id (Primary Key, Auto-increment)
- emergency_id (Foreign Key → emergencies.id)
- volunteer_id (Foreign Key → volunteers.id)
- assigned_at (DateTime)
- accepted_at (DateTime)
- arrived_at (DateTime)
- completed_at (DateTime)
- status (Dropdown): "Assigned", "Accepted", "En Route", "On Site", "Completed", "Declined"
- notes (Long Text): Assignment-specific notes
- rating_given (Number): 1-5 rating from emergency submitter
- feedback (Long Text): Feedback from emergency submitter
```

### 5. Resources Table
```sql
Table: resources
- id (Primary Key, Auto-increment)
- resource_name (Text): "Ambulance", "Fire Truck", "Sandbags", "Generator", etc.
- resource_category (Dropdown): "Medical", "Fire Safety", "Flood Control", "Power", "Transportation", "Communication", "Shelter"
- applicable_emergencies (Multi-Select → emergency_types): Which emergencies this resource helps
- quantity_available (Number)
- quantity_unit (Text): "Units", "Liters", "Kilograms", etc.
- location_latitude (Number)
- location_longitude (Number)
- contact_person (Text)
- contact_phone (Text)
- is_available (Boolean)
- cost_per_unit (Number): Optional cost tracking
- organization_name (Text): Who owns/manages the resource
```

### 6. Safe Zones Table
```sql
Table: safe_zones
- id (Primary Key, Auto-increment)
- zone_name (Text): "City Hall Shelter", "Memorial Hospital", etc.
- zone_type (Dropdown): "Shelter", "Hospital", "Evacuation Center", "Assembly Point"
- applicable_emergencies (Multi-Select → emergency_types)
- latitude (Number)
- longitude (Number)
- address (Text)
- capacity (Number): Maximum people it can handle
- current_occupancy (Number): Current number of people
- contact_phone (Text)
- facilities_available (Multi-Select): "Medical", "Food", "Beds", "Showers", "Pet Care"
- is_currently_open (Boolean)
- operating_hours (Text)
```

### 7. Notifications Table
```sql
Table: notifications
- id (Primary Key, Auto-increment)
- recipient_type (Dropdown): "Volunteer", "Emergency Contact", "Organization"
- recipient_id (Number): ID of recipient
- emergency_id (Foreign Key → emergencies.id)
- notification_type (Dropdown): "SMS", "Email", "Push", "Call"
- message_content (Long Text)
- sent_at (DateTime)
- delivered_at (DateTime)
- read_at (DateTime)
- status (Dropdown): "Pending", "Sent", "Delivered", "Failed", "Read"
```

